{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Versil","id":"148682928434577408","is_bot":0,"username":"versil"},"author_id":"148682928434577408","channel_id":"851856616469823528","content":"?help message","created_at":"2021-06-16T20:05:22.371000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"854813929095692368","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"ArcaniaBot","id":"810907841329627137","is_bot":1,"username":"ArcaniaBot"},"author_id":"810907841329627137","channel_id":"851856616469823528","content":"?message\n`?message (timestamp) (channel) (message text)`\n\nAllows adding a scheduled bot message through a command in Discord instead of files on Dropbox.\nThe timestamp must be either `HH:MM` for messages to be sent once daily,\nor `YY-MM-DD HH:MM` for messages to be sent only once. 24-hour clock, server time.\nThe channel must be either the channel name raw, or the #-link to it.\n\nEverything from the new line after that onwards is treated as the message content.\nIn the message you can put regular Discord mentions, both to specific people and roles, or everyone,\nas well as #-links to channels.\nAlternatively you can use the square brackets notation made for the bot for adding messages directly in files:\n- #[channel-name-or-id] will convert into a link to a channel specified by the name or id in square brackets.\n- @[something] will try to parse the contents either to a role (exact match), or a specific person.\nFor getting specific people, you have options:\n- @[user-id-number] will directly match the person\n- @[current-name-in-server] will match if they have been active in the last 24h (same functionality as ?where)\n- @[name-or-start-of-one] will try to find a member whose username or server nickname matches the input.\nFor example, @[ver] would match Versil if there were no other possibilities.\nUsage of square brackets mention substitutes is msotly there so you don't have to ping a person when setting this.\n\nThe bot will list what it read from your message, including all the mentions it found and parsed.\nThat way you can verify if everything's as you expected, and you then have to confirm it.\nAnything other than \"no\", \"n\", \"0\" or \"nah\" as your response will be treated as confirmation.\n\nThis method also has a variant, `?message interactive` (or `?message assist` or `?message i`).\nThat one will guide you through the process step by step without having to remember what goes where.\n\n**ArcaniaBot** command help *(Maintenance)*\nUse `?help [command]` for more info on a command","created_at":"2021-06-16T20:05:22.716000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"854813930542333982","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
